<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 2 Best in Slot Gear list for Frost Death Knight DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Ulduar, Naxxramas, Obsidian Sanctum, and Eye of Eternity. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c6">Best in Slot Gear for Frost Death Knight DPS Phase 2</span></h2>With the release of both 10m and 25m comes a glut of new items and choices, the vast majority stronger than our pre-raid gear. With split lockouts  the sheer amount of gear you can see every week has increased, and so has the ease of gearing. When looking at item levels, it's important to remember that Hard Mode gear uses item levels a tier higher than its difficulty. With that in mind, we're still typically seeking just for the highest density of stats, with a focus on strength items over nearly any other alternative.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength - is still the absolute best stat for Frost Death Knights, this will not change throughout the expansion.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - to at least 5% - your talent <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=50138/nerves-of-cold-steel">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_dualwield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nerves of Cold Steel</span></a> will give you 3% so you're capped on main hand specials, any point of hit after this will just increase howling blast hit, and auto attacks, but is still powerful.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Crit - is incredibly powerful because of the crit damage amplification of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=50191/guile-of-gorefiend">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv-sword_53.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Guile of Gorefiend</span></a>, making our already hard hitting <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=51425/obliterate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_classicon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obliterate</span></a> even more impressive.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - Expertise has less of a gain for Death Knight's compared to most classes, as our special abilities don't charge us runes if they're dodged, but that strike will still be delayed the lost GCD, and you your white hits can be dodged.</div></li></ol>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;"></div>
<br/>
<br/>This set will put us over the 'soft' cap for hit rating of 8%, but as a dual wield class that's ok, as we still value hit rating highly for our auto attacks. There is an alternative set that is about 17 dps higher, that completely forgoes tier in favor of wearing leather 252 off pieces, I strongly recommend against this set. This DPS gain is purely single target, with it performing much poorer in any cleave or AoE situations, and comes at the cost of taking highly contested agility pieces that are astronomically better on other classes, as well as losing a substantial amount of survivability. <br/>
<br/>
